      "problem": "Sketch the graph of $f(x)=3^x.$",
      "worked_solution": "The graph of $y=3^x$ has a $y$-intercept at $(0,1),$ grows rapidly for $x>0,$ and approaches the asymptote $y=0$ for $x<0.$ \n\nWhen $x=1,$ we have $y=3^1 = 3.$ Therefore, another point on the graph is $(1,3).$ \n\nWe draw the graph through this point as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14194531/assets/4367540979396fd0106204a0f71d9368a70ce3538d8e7239ac250e5fc45644f1.png)",
